CORE
main.c
--unwind 2 --rounds 3 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness --array-rf
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
Nothing writes a[0], and malloc does not zero what it returns, so a[0] can be
anything and the assertion fails. A read-from that gave an unwritten element a
constant -- the element of a zero initialiser, say -- would prove it instead.
Checked by replacing the allocation value with 0 in the selection.
